= Biological database — Technical =

Biological database design must manage identifiers, schemas, sequence/feature coordinate systems, versioning, provenance, controlled vocabularies, evidence codes, cross-references, update/release semantics, APIs and bulk access. Reproducible analyses should record the exact database release or accession state used.

== Modeling / evidence cautions ==
* biological database ≠ flat file collection
* database record ≠ experimentally verified truth
* primary archive ≠ curated derived knowledge by identity

